WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:07.169
Now in this section, we will explore when to use Unreal Game Sync as your front-end user interface.

2
00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:14.460
So Unreal Game Sync provides a graphical front-end user interface to sync Unreal Engine projects from Perforce

3
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.460
with an option to build those projects with Microsoft's Visual Studio compiler.

4
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:25.739
It's a skin for Perforce that allows users to implement version control more easily.

5
00:00:25.739 --> 00:00:33.740
Unreal Game Sync, or UGS, is a tool that promotes code and content integration in collaborative development environments.

6
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:43.539
This enables teammates, distributed over time and distance, to labor on the same projects as it gets updated on the backend.

7
00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:54.539
Basically, Unreal Game Sync can only be used with a custom Unreal Engine build that is stored, maintained, and rebuilt from Perforce through Unreal Game Sync.

8
00:00:54.539 --> 00:01:03.539
Unreal Game Sync users can convert their release version Unreal Engine project to a C++ version Unreal Engine project

9
00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:08.540
and utilize Microsoft Visual Studio to rebuild that engine from Perforce.

10
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.540
When a team is working on a custom Unreal Engine project build,

11
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:19.540
they're working in an environment where code and content is continuously developed and integrated into that project.

12
00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:24.540
One thing to note is that UGS Binaries Depot Path is a global path.

13
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.540
That pathway is listed here.

14
00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.540
So when you set up your own Unreal Game Sync options,

15
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:40.540
make sure that you follow the path shown here to your project binaries and save the UGS binaries inside your custom Perforce build.

16
00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.540
That's it for this section.

17
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:48.540
Next, we will explore the last pillar of the collaborative production pipeline with collaboration tools.

18
00:01:48.540 --> 00:02:17.539
.
